   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 118 of the laws of 1969, relating to a separate union free school district in the town of Greenburgh in the county of Westchester, in relation to clarifying the authority of the Greenburgh North Castle Union Free School District to lease certain properties; and to repeal section 2-a of chapter 118 of the laws of 1969, relating to a separate union free school district in the town of Greenburgh in the county of Westchester",
    "basePrintNo": "S6462",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6462-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §2-a, rpld §2-a, Chap 118 of 1969",
    "lawSection": "Westchester County",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S6462\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to amend chapter 118 of the laws of 1969,\nrelating to a separate union free school district in the town of\nGreenburgh in the county of Westchester, in relation to clarifying the\nauthority of the Greenburgh North Castle Union Free School District to\nlease certain properties; and to repeal section 2-a of chapter 118 of\nthe laws of 1969, relating to a separate union free school district in\nthe town of Greenburgh in the county of Westchester\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\n\nThis legislation will authorize the Greenburgh North Castle union free\nschool district to continue leasing property outside of district\nboundaries for the purpose of providing instruction to students in the\nGreen-burgh North Castle Union Free School District.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSections 1 of the bill amends section 2-a of chapter 118 of the laws\nof 1969, relating to a separate union free school district in the town\nof Greenburgh, county of Westchester, as added by chapter 224 of the\nlaws of 2010, to authorize the Greenburgh North Castle union free\nschool district board of education, subject to the approval of the New\nYork State education department, to lease property located at 45 East\nGainsborg Avenue in the village of West Harrison in Westchester\nCounty, for the purpose of providing instruction to students enrolled\nin the school district.\n\nSection 2 states that Section 2-a of chapter 118 of the laws of 1969,\nrelating to a separate union free school district in the town of\nGreenburgh in the county of Westchester, as added by chapter 226 of\nthe laws of 2010, is repealed.\n\nSection 3 provides that the actions of the board of education\nregarding lease arrangements at the site in West Harrison are ratified\nand validated notwithstanding its location outside the boundaries of\nthe school district.\n\nSection 4 is the effective date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nThe Greenburgh North Castle Union Free School District (the\n\"District\") is a special act district that currently operates programs\nto serve special needs students. In 2011, the District opened the\nREACH Program, commonly referred to as the REACH Academy, in West\nHarrison which now serves approximately 68 students. Since the present\nlocation is outside of the District's physical boundaries, the\nauthorization to lease space for the REACH Academy has been secured\nthrough a yearly approval process by the State Education Department.\nThis legislation will authorize the District, subject to the approval\nof the State Education Department to continue providing these\nimportant student services without interruption for the duration of\nthe lease.\n\nLegislation authorizing the District to lease space outside the\nDistrict's properties for its program was previously approved in 2010\n(A.8871-C/S.1789).\n\nLegislation authorizing the District to lease the space which is the\nsubject of this legislation was vetoed by the Governor in 2013 since\nthe legislation also included language that would have expanded the\nschool district boundaries to include the leased premises (A.6721-\nWS.5829). The Governor's veto memo clearly stated that authority to\nlease and utilize property outside the district's boundaries had been\ngranted in the past for this school and other special act schools but\nthe expansion of its boundaries would have a fiscal impact that should\ntake place in the context of the budget.\n\nThis legislation will only authorize the District, subject to the\napproval of the State Education Department, to lease the property for\nthe continuation of its school services.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNew bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS :\n\nNone\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
